td width=129 valign=top style='width:96.9pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt'>Unit<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=205 valign=top style='width:153.6pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><b><span\r\n  lang=EN-US style='font-size:12.0pt'>Bio. Ref. Interval<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr style='height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <td width=330 valign=top style='width:247.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'><\/td>\r\n  <td width=84 valign=top style='width:63.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.5pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=129 valign=top style='width:96.9pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.5pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=205 valign=top style='width:153.6pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.5pt'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr style='height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <td width=330 valign=top style='width:247.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:11.0pt'>PARATHYROID\r\n  HORMONE (PTH) - INTACT<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=84 valign=top style='width:63.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>114.30<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=129 valign=top style='width:96.9pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>pg\/ml<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=205 valign=top style='width:153.6pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:12.7pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:11.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>11.1 \u2013 79.5<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n <tr style='height:16.65pt'>\r\n  <td width=330 valign=top style='width:247.5pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:16.65pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>Methodology : CLIA<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=84 valign=top style='width:63.0pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:16.65pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=129 valign=top style='width:96.9pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:16.65pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n  <td width=205 valign=top style='width:153.6pt;padding:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\r\n  height:16.65pt'>\r\n  <p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center'><span lang=EN-US\r\n  style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n  <\/td>\r\n <\/tr>\r\n<\/table>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>COMMENT<\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:-67.5pt'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u00a0<\/span><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>The so-called\r\nintact PTH is the most frequently ordered parathyroid hormone test,it regulates\r\nthe serum calcium through its effects on bone, kidney, and intestine.PTH\r\ninfluences bone remodeling, which is an ongoing process in which bone tissue is\r\nalternately resorbed and rebuilt over time. PTH is secreted in response to low\r\nblood serum calcium (Ca2+) levels. PTH indirectly stimulates osteoclast\r\nactivity within the bone matrix (osteon), in an effort to release more ionic\r\ncalcium (Ca2+) into the blood to elevate a low serum calcium level. The bones\r\nact as a (metaphorical) &quot;bank of calcium&quot; from which the body can\r\nmake &quot;withdrawals&quot; as needed to keep the amount of calcium in the\r\nblood at appropriate levels despite the ever-present challenges of metabolism,\r\nstress, and nutritional variations. PTH is &quot;a key that unlocks the bank\r\nvault&quot; to remove the calcium.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:-67.5pt'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:-67.5pt'><span lang=EN-US\r\nstyle='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>PTH is secreted\r\nprimarily by the chief cells of the parathyroid glands.Its action is opposed by\r\nthe hormone calcitonin<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Clinical\r\nUse <\/span><\/b><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u2022&nbsp;Diagnose&nbsp;hyperparathyroidism\r\n\u2022&nbsp;Monitor&nbsp;severity&nbsp;of&nbsp;secondary&nbsp;hyperparathyroidism&nbsp;in&nbsp;chronic&nbsp;renal&nbsp;failure\r\n\u2022&nbsp;Discriminate&nbsp;primary&nbsp;hyperparathyroidism&nbsp;from&nbsp;tumor&nbsp;hypercalcemia<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Increased\r\nLevels<\/span><\/b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\r\n<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u2022&nbsp;Primary&nbsp;hyperparathyroidism\r\n<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u2022&nbsp;Secondary&nbsp;hyperparathyroidism\r\n<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u2022&nbsp;Renal&nbsp;failure\r\n<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u2022&nbsp;Pseudohypoparathyroidism<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Decreased\r\nLevels<\/span><\/b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\r\n<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u2022&nbsp;Hypoparathyroidism\r\n<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-size:9.0pt;font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>\u2022&nbsp;Hypercalcemia&nbsp;of&nbsp;malignancy<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><b><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>Notes<\/span><\/b><span\r\nlang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'> <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>1.\r\nTest results should be interpreted in conjunction with serum calcium and\r\nphosphorus levels, and clinical findings. <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>2.\r\nElevated PTH with normal serum calcium levels may be indicative of Secondary\r\ncauses of hyperparathyroidism like vitamin D deficiency. It may not always be\r\nindicative of Primary hyperparathyroidism. <\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>3.\r\nPTH is secreted in a pulsatile manner with an overall circadian rhythm\r\ncharacterized by a nocturnal rise.<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US style='font-family:\"Bookman Old Style\",serif'>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal><span lang=EN-US>&nbsp;<\/span><\/p>\r\n\r\n<\/div>","page":{"size":"612.0pt 792.0pt","margin":"148.5pt 90.0pt 72.0pt 27.0pt"}}